ist is not only to have a purely  personal but a social status and  production here's what's actually being  denied here this is all social meaning  that it's part of social processes the  reason why a factory owner can actually  operate his or her factory and hire  people is because there's a whole bunch  of things in society actually propping  that up and making it possible for them  to do that there is no such thing  according to Marx within bourgeois  property as the self-made man there is  in pre bourgeois property but that  becomes rarer and rarer and rarer and  one of the things that people often do  is a Tate bourgeois property and they  pretend like it's pre-modern property  when it's not really so so it says  capital is a social power when capital  is converted into common property into  the property of all the members of  society personal property is not  transformed into social property it's  only putting it back where it was  originally it loses its class character  so he says let's now take wage labour  the average price is the minimum wage so  whatever the worker is getting by his or  her labor they're never able to get  ahead as a matter of fact they're  falling further and further behind the  entire time so in bourgeois  Society what does this tell you about  people living labor is but it means to  increase accumulated labour what does  that mean the living labor that's going  into creating this wealth here is being  put back into the system to now create  mechanisms of control over that very  labor in communist Society says  accumulated labor is but it means to  widen to enrich to promote the existence  of the labor so now notice what he's  saying here is that if we're going to  switch from bourgeois property to  communist property you're not going back  to this you're actually still  maintaining some sort of surplus but  that surplus would now go back in part  into here even better wages and the  surplus is going back into taking care  of the condition of the laborer so  instead of making somebody's mansion  bigger it builds a park instead of  putting a new brick face on the bank  maybe it creates a new Coliseum where  people can go and not pay eighty bucks a  ticket or whatever it is to go see a  sporting event but go for free the idea  is that you still have some sort of  surplus being generated but that surplus  is being used for socially useful ends  for the benefit of the working class not  for the benefit of the ruling  parasitical capitalist class so he goes  on he says another way to think about  this in bourgeois society the past  dominates the present the fact that you  took surplus capital out from before and  now you have wealth and now you can  reinvest it means that the past  dominates the present in cognitive  society the present dominates the past  you're replacing the old ways in words  on society capital is independent and  has individuality but what about the  living person the living person is  depend  it has no individuality so it radically  changes the ordering between wealth and  people people should be higher than  wealth  according to to those of you so what do  we have to say about this mark says yes  we do intend to abolish property  bourgeois property we're gonna make  social property social and he points out  a few other things too he says you know  if you're gonna criticize us for  abolishing private property keep in mind  not everybody has private property as a  matter of fact most people don't he says  in your existing society private  property has already done a way for  we've done away with for nine-tenths of  the population its existence for the few  is due to its non-existence in the hands  of those 9/10 so if we're abolishing it  it's not really hurting other people so  much because we're actually doing  something that's good for the majority  another interesting objection that he  considers with respect to that is that  if we abolish property altogether then  nobody's go